    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nVersion 2 of the owner identity, implemented as small localized edits (six files, each change a line or two in a low-complexity function):\n\n**Identifiers rederived with a `V2` tag** (so every one changes and no V1 value recurs):\n- `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` \u2014 the region code *inside* the memberId is now the plain region prefixed with `V2` (e.g. `V2NSW2716E6609E7`). V1 memberIds started with a region letter, so no V2 value can equal a V1 value.\n- `IdentityKey.java` \u2014 mixes `\"V2|\"` into the SHA-256 preimage.\n- `HouseholdId.java` \u2014 mixes `\"V2|\"` into the SHA-256 preimage.\n\n**Locality stays plain** \u2014 `Locality.of` is untouched, so `locality` (`NSW`), `timezone`, and the owner segment's derived region remain the plain region code. The `V2` tag appears only inside the identifiers.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`):\n- `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` moved under a nested `identity` object and removed from the top level. MapStruct auto-builds the nested DTO via `target = \"identity.*\"`.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` of `2`.\n\n**Audit event** (`SaveOwner.java`) \u2014 moved to schema version 2: added `\"schemaVersion\":2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the V2 identity (its region kept plain, e.g. `STANDARD_METRO`).\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. `RespondWithOwner` and `OwnerSegment` needed no edits \u2014 the ownerSegment field keeps its plain-region derivation. Verified end to end: the audit log now emits `{\"schemaVersion\":2,...,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",...,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",...}` and the acceptance test's structural contract (`apiVersion: 2`, nested `identity`, no top-level identity fields) passes.",
