    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml`. Every step from `build` onward runs under a single `transaction` governance (one commit at the end); `checkIdempotency` runs before the transaction.\n\n**Gate (whole file):** `authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 request is rejected (403 via `AuthorizationDeniedException`) unless the caller has that role.\n\nThen, in pipeline order:\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 *validation / short-circuit.* Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key already produced an owner, throws `IdempotentCreateException(existingId)` to return the prior owner instead of creating a duplicate. (No transaction, read-only.)\n\n**2. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 *validation + side-effects.*\n- Requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and an address in either form (`addressLine1` or `address`). Any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(list)` (400).\n- Maps the `OwnerFieldsDto` to an `Owner`.\n- Sets `registrationDate` to `nextBusinessDay(...)` of the supplied date, or of today if none was supplied. Publishes the `Owner`.\n\n**3. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 *validation.* If `registrationDate` is after `nextBusinessDay(today)` \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). (Same-day/absent accepted.)\n\n**4. `ValidateOwnerPostcode`** \u2014 *validation.* If a postcode is present it must be exactly 4 digits, and for a known city region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) fall in that range \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException([\"postcode\"])` (400). Absent postcode is left untouched.\n\n**5. `NormalizeOwnerAddress`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, expands abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE); rewrites `addressLine1/2` and `address` in place. If blank after normalization \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException([\"address\"])` (400).\n\n**6. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Rewrites `telephone` to E.164 in place. If it can't form valid E.164 \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException([\"telephone\"])` (400).\n\n**7. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 *validation + side-effect.* Email optional (null/blank left untouched). If present must match the email regex, else 400; rejects disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 400. Otherwise lower-cased in place.\n\n**8. `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`** \u2014 *validation.* Computes `IdentityKey` = SHA-256 of `E164(telephone) | lower(email) | soundex(lastName)`. If any non-deleted other owner shares it \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409).\n\n**9. `RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 *validation.* If the owner's city (trimmed, case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n**10. `RejectOwnerDailyLimit`** \u2014 *validation.* If \u2265 100 owners already share this `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n**11. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `customerCode` = `\"V2\" + region + 2-digit fiscal year + hash8 + Luhn check digit` (hash8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`).\n\n**12. `DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect.* If that code collides with an existing owner's, appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\n**13. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effects.* Persists via `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns id). Computes namesake count and membership level, then emits three log records: an `AUDIT` \"owner created\" line, an `AUDIT` immutable structured JSON event (schema v2, incrementing `EVENT_SEQ`, `OWNER_CREATED`), and a `NOTIFY` welcome line.\n\n**14. `RecordIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Stores the new owner's id under the request's `Idempotency-Key` in `IdempotencyStore` (so repeats return this owner).\n\n**15. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect (response assembly).* Maps to `OwnerDto` and enriches it: `namesakeCount`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel` (household-capped), `bulkSignupWarning`, and `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. Sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nA few things worth flagging:\n- The request DTO is bound with `@RequestBody` **only** (no `@Valid`), so all field validation is the manual logic in `BuildOwner`/normalizers \u2014 Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` does not run here.\n- Idempotency lookup (step 1) is the only step outside the transaction; the record (step 14) and everything from step 2 commit together at the end."
